{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183895,"nonce":"L3kbcSZ70sXj5Z1aESWeA27P0UY=","title":"ADR-0062 s6: a Step Pod receives its Workspace as a per-Step PVC, with soft zone preference","message":"Wire the executor: per-Step PersistentVolume (NFS source) + PersistentVolumeClaim, mounted at `/workspace`. The Step Pod holds **no privilege, no capability and no PSA exception**. When an Export is available the `scarab-wsfetch` init container is not used and the drain-side `exec` tar tunnel is not used.\n\n**Delivery as a PVC rather than an inline `nfs:` volume is load-bearing, not stylistic.** Measured: PodSecurity `restricted` denies inline `nfs:` and allows `persistentVolumeClaim` (ADR-0062's PSA table).\n\nZone affinity is **preferred, never required** (part 4): Scarab picks the replica at launch, prepares the Export there, and expresses a preference. Cross-AZ is slower and metered, never wrong. Hard-pinning is explicitly rejected — it fights spot capacity and silently amends the placement overlays ADR-0055 makes the operator's to own.\n\n\n- [ ] A Step with `needs:` runs against an Export with no fetcher init container and no `exec` tar on either side\n- [ ] The step container keeps ADR-0039's full restricted baseline; the Pod is admissible under PodSecurity `restricted`\n- [ ] `/workspace` is unchanged as a path — no authored pipeline needs editing\n- [ ] Zone affinity is `preferred`, and a Pod that lands out-of-zone still works\n- [ ] `scarab-wsfetch` and the HTTP CAS path still work as the no-Export fallback (local executor, and modes without an Export) — they are demoted, not deleted\n- [ ] Verified on the live kind/colima tier, with the fixture panicking rather than skipping when the tier is opted in\n\n\n- s5 (needs a real export to mount)","files":null}]}